# A COMPOSED DEMAND EQUALS THE SUM OF ITS CONVERTED PARTS, LESS WHAT THE COMPOSER ELIMINATED.
# One row per fusion that OWES that equality, with a verdict on each.
#
#     x_composed = F Φ x_parts − e
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ THE MODEL'S HEADLINE EQUATION HAD NO CONFORMANCE RULE UNTIL NOW, AND THAT IS THE GAP
#    THIS FILLS. composition/fused.sqlc has computed the sum, the filed figure and an `agrees`
#    verdict for as long as it has existed, and exactly one caller read it: matrices.sqlc, a
#    psql tour that PRINTS it. examples/matrices.rs recomputes the product in Rust instead. So
#    the one equation the whole repository is built to check was asserted by an example and a
#    test, and by nothing that reports/violations.sqlc or reports/coverage.sqlc could see.
#
# ⛔⛔ THE POPULATION IS ALREADY CORRECT AND MUST NOT BE WIDENED. composition/fused.sqlc inner
#    joins composition/owed_equality.sqlc, so a fusion suspended on either ground is ABSENT
#    here rather than counted as a pass. Adding the suspended rows would report a document that
#    declined to claim the equality as one that satisfied it, which is the exact defect
#    asrt:StatedEliminations was added to prevent.
#
# ⭐ IT IS THE DEMAND EQUALITY AND NOTHING ELSE. composition/fused.sqlc pins `quantity` at
#   `demand` and says so in its own column; six nameplate eliminations and two draw eliminations
#   are filed in this corpus and no rule reads them. A nameplate sibling is a second file over a
#   second fused relation, not a widening of this one.
#
# ⛔ THIS SPANS TWO DOCUMENTS, WHICH IS WHY NO GRAMMAR CAN STATE IT. The parts are in one filing
#   and the composed figure is in another; XSD 1.0 cannot follow the reference, let alone add up
#   what is on the other end.
-- asrt:Fusion/asrt:Part summed against the composed pm:Layer/pm:Demand, via composition/fused.sqlc.
SELECT r.rule, p.filing, p.layer, p.violates, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(checks/roster.sqlc)
) r
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT f.composition AS filing, f.composed_layer AS layer,
           NOT f.agrees AS violates,
           format('parts less eliminations give [%s, %s, %s]; the filing states [%s, %s, %s]',
                  f.computed_low, f.computed_mode, f.computed_high,
                  f.filed_low, f.filed_mode, f.filed_high) AS detail
    FROM (
        :compose(composition/fused.sqlc)
    ) f
) p ON true
WHERE r.slug = 'fusion_sum_disagrees'
